# The Act 1 midpoint report, the road out, and the Act 1 end scene.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2849–2900.
# Scene: scenes/chapter2/ch2_ending.tscn.
# The report seeds faction reputation (Hearth / Archive / Continuity); it is
# not the Axis 2 lock. The road sets Act 1's pace (early / on time / late).

~ report
Kaelen (Internal): Everything I've found. Two fragments, the tower logs, what was under the market. Somebody who isn't me should have a copy.
? Kaelen (Internal): Who gets the report?
- Oakhaven's and Ironhold's councils. The people who have to live with it. => report_local
- The archivists in the Wastes. People who keep records properly. => report_archive
- Ironhold command. People who can act on it tomorrow. => report_command

~ report_local
set act1_report_local
[if has_elara] Elara: Mara's going to read every word of that, and then tell everyone it was her idea.

~ report_archive
set act1_report_archive
Kaelen (Internal): Somebody out there writes things down for a living. I hope they're honest about it.

~ report_command
set act1_report_command
Brask: I'll read it. I might even agree with some of it.

~ road_out
Kaelen (Internal): The next trace points at the Fractured Wastes.
[if ch2_seraphina_recruited] Seraphina: Three ways there. The safe road's long. The old server road's short, and it isn't safe. The caravan route depends on Oakhaven's bridge.
[if not ch2_seraphina_recruited] Rook: Three roads to the Wastes. Long and safe, short and stupid, or the caravan, if Oakhaven's bridge is still up.
[if ch1_bridge_fell] Kaelen (Internal): It isn't. So, two roads.
? Kaelen (Internal): Which way?
- The old server road. Fast, and unstable. => pace_early
- The safe road. => pace_on_time
- [if not ch1_bridge_fell] The caravan route, with the traders. => pace_late

~ pace_early
set act1_pace_early

~ pace_on_time
set act1_pace_on_time

~ pace_late
set act1_pace_late
Rook: Caravan leaves at noon. I'm on it. You're paying for your own cart.

# The Act 1 end scene, on Ironhold's outer bridge.
~ end
[if ch2_seraphina_recruited] => end_recruited
[if ch2_seraphina_stayed] => end_stayed
[if ch2_seraphina_rejected] => end_rejected
=> end_horizon

~ end_recruited
do seraphina_joins
Seraphina: My banner's folded in your pack. Don't use it as a pillow.
=> end_horizon

~ end_stayed
Seraphina: Bring me back something useful. Not just stories.
Kaelen: Like what? What counts as useful?
Seraphina: Answers. Real ones.
Kaelen: Those are rare out here.
Seraphina: Then bring coffee. I'd settle for coffee.
=> end_horizon

~ end_rejected
Seraphina: I hope I'm wrong about you.
Kaelen: Me too. I really do.
Elara: Well. That was comfortable for everyone.
Kaelen: Extremely. Let's never do it again.
=> end_horizon

~ end_horizon
[if ch1_bridge_fell] Kaelen (Internal): There's a refugee wagon coming up the Oakhaven road. The bridge. Of course.
[if ch1_bridge_saved] Kaelen (Internal): A trade wagon's heading down toward Oakhaven. Over mismatched planks, I bet. Holding, though.
[if ch2_medicine_late] Kaelen (Internal): The infirmary bells are still ringing.
[if ch2_medicine_early] Kaelen (Internal): Every light in the lower city is on.
do sky_seam
Kaelen: That way. Past the hills.
Elara: You say that like the sky's pointing.
Kaelen: It is. It's been pointing all day.
